  "details": "It may sound a bit unreasonable but because the parameters now also have the lerp function, single bit float can be used for optimization of toggles that use transitions. (Toggle transitions can be used for example for cloth dissolves.) Normally to have a toggle with transition you would need an animator layer with two states transitioning between each other just for the one toggle. Now it can be done using float parameter with lerp set to custom duration, which will be used in direct blend tree. Only disadvantage is that these toggles will require 2x more synced bits because float can be set to minimum of 2 bits.\n\nThe 1 bit float could still support setting it to be signed/unsigned which will only change if the two possible synced values would be either -1 and 1 or 0 and 1.",
